{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"Codeby.RIGStats","latestVersion":"1.53.0","media":{"icons":[],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Hardware monitor and control center for Windows gaming PCs","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/dvalfrid/rigstats/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Hardware monitor and control center for Windows gaming PCs","license":"MIT","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/dvalfrid/rigstats/blob/main/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"RIGStats is a free, open-source hardware monitor and control center for Windows gaming PCs.\nLive CPU, GPU, RAM, storage, network and motherboard sensors on a secondary display, as\nfloating panels, in the desktop wallpaper or as an in-game overlay.\n\nProfiles (Silent, Balanced, Gaming, Eco and your own) set the Windows power plan, fan curves,\nAMD Ryzen and Radeon/GeForce power limits, RGB lighting (ASUS Aura Sync, Windows Dynamic\nLighting, Philips Hue) and the desktop background or Wallpaper Engine — and can switch by\nthemselves while a program runs. Fan curves run in a background service, so they keep working\nwith the app closed.\n\nNo telemetry. No accounts. No cloud. MIT license.","moniker":"rigstats","name":"RIGStats","packageUrl":"https://rigstats.app","publisher":"codeby.se","publisherUrl":"https://rigstats.app","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/dvalfrid/rigstats/releases/tag/v1.53.0","tags":["hardware","monitor","system-monitor","cpu","gpu","temperature","fan-control","rgb","aura-sync","overlay","gaming","dashboard","profiles"]}},"longDescription":"RIGStats is a free, open-source hardware monitor and control center for Windows gaming PCs.\nLive CPU, GPU, RAM, storage, network and motherboard sensors on a secondary display, as\nfloating panels, in the desktop wallpaper or as an in-game overlay.\n\nProfiles (Silent, Balanced, Gaming, Eco and your own) set the Windows power plan, fan curves,\nAMD Ryzen and Radeon/GeForce power limits, RGB 